{"id":"resp_b0e6a42435b6063b","created_at":1795591103,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_a2d3252b9febfddd","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need to produce JSON with assessment, issues, questions per schema. We must evaluate candidate SHACL: version 2 same as version 1, just prefix change : @prefix : <https://example.org/shapes#> . In previous candidate, nltl prefix was https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#. In version 2, the nltl prefix is https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#. So same. The shape defines CategoryAShipShape with targetClass nltl:ship etc. Need to check against regulation and schema. The regulation says Category A ship means ship designed for operation in polar waters in at least medium first‑year ice, which may include old ice inclusions. The shape enforces two properties: shipCategory = polarShipCategoryA; designIceCondition = mediumFirstYearIceWithPossibleOldIceInclusions. Those IRIs exist in schema: E14/E25 etc define polarShipCategoryA as concept; E38/E64/E117/E155 define mediumFirstYearIceWithPossibleOldIceInclusions. So mapping seems okay.\n\nBut we need to assess if any missing constraints: The regulation also mentions \"polar waters\" and maybe other conditions (ice in polar waters) but representation may need path for location/polar waters? Not required per spec? The shape just ensures category and design ice condition, not location. The regulation says \"ship designed for operation in polar waters\". The shape does not enforce that the ship operates in polar waters, only design ice condition. However the \"polar waters\" condition might be implicit in category A definition; but from schema, there is no property about operating region. No RDF property for \"operating in polar waters\" is given. So missing constraint could be flagged as context question: missing representation of \"operation in polar waters\". That is a missing representation in schema: no path representing operational region. So we should raise a question.\n\nAlso check that the shape uses sh:hasValue for designIceCondition, which forces exact value. That's appropriate.\n\nPotential issues: Prefix for shapes uses example.org, but shape IRI is not in declared schema (they expected shape IRI maybe in same namespace as others?). Not required.\n\nCheck for sh:property needs sh:minCount 1 maybe? Not required because hasValue ensures presence? In SHACL, sh:hasValue does not require property to exist; but if property missing, constraint not triggered? Actually sh:hasValue means the property must contain that value; but if missing property, the constraint will not pass? According to SHACL, a shape with sh:hasValue will fail if the property is missing or does not contain that value. So okay.\n\nThus the only material gap is missing representation for \"operation in polar waters\". That's a context question (schema missing). Must ask question: missing property path for location/polarWaters, why matters, kind: schema.\n\nThus assessment should be HUMAN_REVIEW_REQUIRED because a question is present. Since there is at least one question, we cannot APPROVE.\n\nIssues: Any code issues? The code seems fine syntactically; no errors. So no issues.\n\nThus output JSON with assessment \"HUMAN_REVIEW_REQUIRED\", empty issues array, one question.\n\nProvide question fields: missing, why, kind, reference?, section?, evidence.\n\nMissing: representation of operational region (polar waters) e.g., property like nltl:operatingRegion or similar. Why: regulation requires ship designed for operation in polar waters; without capturing that, SHACL cannot enforce the full obligation. Kind: schema. Reference: maybe regulation clause \"IMO-001 §2.1\". Section maybe \"2.1\". Evidence can reference E191 which includes clause text. Provide evidence array with reference to E191 (source). Use just string \"E191\". location: maybe lines of candidate where issue arises? Could be line of shape where property constraints start, but location not about code because it's missing. For issues, location required, but this is a question, not issue, so location not needed. For question, location not required.\n\nThus produce JSON.","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_8f62634430cc5b80","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"{\n  \"assessment\": \"HUMAN_REVIEW_REQUIRED\",\n  \"issues\": [],\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"missing\": \"A property/path representing the ship's intended operational region (e.g., polar waters) such as nltl:operatingRegion or equivalent.\",\n      \"why\": \"The regulatory definition (IMO‑001 §2.1) specifies that a Category A ship is designed for operation in polar waters. Without a representation of the operational region, the SHACL shape cannot fully enforce the obligation, leaving a material gap in the compliance model.\",\n      \"kind\": \"schema\",\n      \"reference\": \"IMO‑001 §2.1\",\n      \"section\": \"2.1\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"E191\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":1.0,"background":false,"max_output_tokens":16000,"max_tool_calls":null,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"auto","status":"completed","text":null,"top_logprobs":null,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":32471,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":64,"cache_write_tokens":32400,"input_tokens_per_turn":[32471],"cached_tokens_per_turn":[64]},"output_tokens":1014,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":839,"tool_output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_per_turn":[1014],"tool_output_tokens_per_turn":[0]},"total_tokens":33485},"user":null,"presence_penalty":0.0,"frequ